    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0103" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg69"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            Denby.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1484.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 2774, of the 10th ultimo, inclosing a copy of a note addressed by
                    you to the Tsung-li Yamên on that date, demanding that viceroys, governors, and
                    all other officials be held responsible by the Chinese Government for
                    antiforeign riots occurring within their jurisdiction, and punished
                    accordingly.</p>
                <p>The Department approves generally the ground taken in your note to the Tsung-li
                    Yamên.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
